# ============================================================================
# MISSION 4: CRITICAL FAILURE - SCENARIO FILE
# ============================================================================
# Break Escape - Season 1: The Architect's Shadow
#
# Grid-scale battery energy storage attack. ENTROPY's Critical Mass cell has
# infiltrated the Albion Energy Storage facility (200 MWh lithium-ion BESS) and
# compromised the BMS/SCADA to falsify thermal sensors and disable the hydrogen
# venting and Emergency Shutdown (ESD) interlocks — driving the battery racks
# toward catastrophic thermal runaway. At 0800 the racks tip into a chain fire /
# hydrogen explosion, taking the grid down for 240,000 people and levelling the
# site. Cross-cell coordination with Social Fabric revealed.
#
# Setting/assets adapted from sis02_energy (battery hall, SCADA control room,
# rack status panels, H2 detector, analog thermometer, ESD pushbutton).
#
# ENTROPY Cell: Critical Mass
# Mission Type: Infrastructure Crisis / Tactical Response
# Difficulty: Intermediate (Mission 4)
#
# NEW MECHANICS:
# - Combat encounters with hostile NPCs
# - Stage-based urgency system (no timer)
# - SCADA / BMS investigation (falsified telemetry vs physical instrument)
# - Multi-vector attack disabling + Emergency Shutdown (ESD) minigame
# - Critical tactical choices
#
# ROOM LAYOUT (PASS 3 puzzle chains -- see PUZZLE_CHAINS_PLAN.md):
#
#   main_entrance (guard)
#     +-- S -> operations_office (Vance: Level 1 card is CLONED off him -- m03 cloner)
#                +-- S -> security_office            locker [key] spare Level 1; reader export (clue)
#                +-- E -> scada_control_room
#                           +-- E -> battery_hall_1 (Cipher, optional; Duty Round Panel = Vance's print)
#                                      +-- S -> engineering_workshop  [rfid: Level 2]  VM, flag station,
#                                      |                              OptiGrid tool case [key] -> fingerprint kit
#                                      +-- E -> battery_hall_2 / inverter room  [rfid: Level 1]  (Relay: drops Level 2)
#                                                 +-- S -> plant_room  [biometric: Robert Vance]  (Voltage + Static, ESD)
#                                                            +-- E -> loading_dock  (go-bag [key]); Voltage's escape route
#
# Chain: the plant reader is met in Hall 2 before the workshop can open (its card is
# Relay's), the kit is in the workshop, and the print is on the way back through Hall 1.
#
# Layout reworked 2026-08-21 (ALIGNMENT_PLAN Phase 1b) to clear four world-space
# overlaps. Two structural changes, both of which also tightened the lock chain:
#   * engineering_workshop had a SECOND door from scada_control_room that bypassed
#     Cipher entirely; it now hangs only off battery_hall_1.
#   * plant_room hung off battery_hall_1, so it sat next to the hall before the
#     player had ever met Relay; it now hangs off battery_hall_2, which is what
#     makes the Master keycard a genuine gate.
# Verify with: ruby scripts/validate_scenario.rb (world-space overlap check).
#
# PASS 2 (playtest D1): scada -> battery_hall_1 was a SOUTH connection, and the
# doorway opened onto the hall's solid north wall. The engine placed the 20-wide
# hall under the 10-wide control room using the parity of the control room's
# ORIGIN (rooms.js positionSouthSingle), but placed each door by the parity of
# the SHARED WALL (doors.js placeSouthDoorSingle / placeNorthDoorSingle).
# room_control_1x2gu is 10x6, a stacking height of 1 grid unit (odd), so the two
# parities disagree and the doors land 320px apart. The validator checks overlap,
# not door alignment. The hall now hangs EAST of the control room: E/W pairs are
# top-aligned and both doors sit at top + 2.5 tiles, so they always line up.
# Every connection was re-checked against a port of the engine's BFS and door
# placement (all aligned, no overlaps).
# ============================================================================

# ERB Helper Methods
require 'base64'

def base64_encode(text)
  Base64.strict_encode64(text)
end

